BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.20 Tm (explains why switching mistakes are dangerous rather than cosmetic: at high voltages even air can act like a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.97 Tm (conductor, so a break in a line can keep carrying current as an arc, which is why breakers lean on vacuum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 500.75 Tm (at lower voltage and oil or gas dielectric at higher voltage [7Q-aVBv7PWM @ 00:03:31]. The lesson from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 485.52 Tm (walk is that a yard can be energized-ready on paper and still carry a strap, a fuse or a conduit run that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 470.30 Tm (defeats the protection design.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.07 Tm (On the design side, the failures cluster in a predictable window. Keentel Engineering places the risk between) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.85 Tm (the 30% and 60% packages [GAM0L1fXtiA @ 00:15:03], and names grounding and duct-bank collisions as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 424.62 Tm (the most common rework caught in the 60% 3D clash review that also supports a Class 2 cost estimate) Tj ET
